Yeah, but who'd want to write sudge a mess?  Probably could be calculated
from the following scheme, which would add to the % from chests and
rooms (1/1200 after the magnitude shift you pointed out)

%(wow in shop) = A * B * C * D

A = % of a shop per level (varies with depth in donjon)
B = % of shops having wands + (% of general shop items that are wands)
C = average # of wands in shop
D = % of wands that are WoW

I don't have the source and can't supply the numbers, but guesstimates
are A = 0.2 for pre-castle (Averaging in Gnomish Shopping Mall); B = 0.1
(There's ring, potion, armor, weapon, general, book, food, wand, hardware,
and maybe others.  General most common, it seems, so~10%) C = 20 (4x4 shop)
D = 0.005, for %(wowis) = 0.002 or 1 in 500 per level for shops.  This 
seems a bit high, as all (both) WoWs I've found outside the castle have
not been in shops, where here it look s like shops are 2.4 times more 
likely to have WoW than non-shop rooms.

